    },
    {
      "id": "M4U-9231-IN-Q-S41",
      "kind_group": "quick",
      "model": {
        "kind": "logic",
        "answer": "A",
        "reason": "<p>Only A derives the next claim from the stated hypothesis and the new term.</p>"
      },
      "contentSha256": "1c79bf29d365c1deafb1df30bfd5bb7b05efd4382415435572c66de8362787ba"
    },
    {
      "id": "M4U-9231-IN-Q-S42",
      "kind_group": "quick",
      "model": {
        "kind": "logic",
        "answer": "B",
        "reason": "<p>P(4) starts the chain at its permitted first transition; a later isolated case does not establish earlier cases.</p>"
      },
      "contentSha256": "bed5491e49428c30eec20c98b97e0e8007211cef4ceed23c489ff464db1d65e2"
    },
    {
      "id": "M4U-9231-IN-Q-D41",
      "kind_group": "quick",
      "model": {
        "kind": "logic",
        "answer": "C",
        "reason": "<p>2(k+1)−2k=2, so two differentiations are required.</p>"
      },
      "contentSha256": "6347ecdf86964f88825a625b35da89808aefe26060dd198d7f92530545792314"
    },
    {
      "id": "M4U-9231-IN-Q-D42",
      "kind_group": "quick",
      "model": {
        "kind": "logic",
        "answer": "D",
        "reason": "<p>(n−1)! is defined in the usual factorial notation at n=1; n=0 would introduce (−1)!.</p>"
      },
      "contentSha256": "6150ab5e0cfe342601100409cbb1bda265b01b3aa1ff230dcf86921d21b08d55"
    },
    {
      "id": "M4U-9231-IN-Q-R41",
      "kind_group": "quick",
      "model": {
        "kind": "logic",
        "answer": "B",
        "reason": "<p>Both initial cases and the paired implication carry every later term.</p>"
      },
      "contentSha256": "27299eace304c430fa75a0319bdced771c214a3dd2d23f72d2f1b417fcd5b6e3"
    },
    {
      "id": "M4U-9231-IN-Q-R42",
      "kind_group": "quick",
      "model": {
        "kind": "logic",
        "answer": "A",
        "reason": "<p>The sign controls the inequality direction, and a zero denominator would make the next term undefined.</p>"
      },
      "contentSha256": "6e6eda15f3eaaddcfb947870ba3f979c640729bb92513ebde6da34bacf1d547d"
    },
    {
      "id": "M4U-9231-IN-Q-M41",
      "kind_group": "quick",
      "model": {
        "kind": "logic",
        "answer": "C",
        "reason": "<p>\\(A^{k}A=A^{k+1}\\). The full matrix product must be calculated.</p>"
      },
      "contentSha256": "5521991a0c122321c3ab68eb7bbaff1681187c4a69f9c5f3c5958192d3e55ea7"
    },
    {
      "id": "M4U-9231-IN-Q-M42",
      "kind_group": "quick",
      "model": {
        "kind": "logic",
        "answer": "D",
        "reason": "<p>General A and B need not commute; a proof cannot move B past A without justification.</p>"
      },
      "contentSha256": "bb39cded2d5a62e91e6ce6dc935c72c3e8629e5a73d7684093702a958b516304"
    },
    {
      "id": "M4U-9231-IN-Q-V41",
      "kind_group": "quick",
      "model": {
        "kind": "logic",
        "answer": "B",
        "reason": "<p>The expression is \\(7(3q+k^{2})\\), and the bracket is an integer.</p>"
      },
      "contentSha256": "4dfd30cd15a70c33a1f6f1bdb37a6f8c2bbcb3672d79b9e4c9ff5471dc0190c3"
    },
    {
      "id": "M4U-9231-IN-Q-V42",
      "kind_group": "quick",
      "model": {
        "kind": "logic",
        "answer": "A",
        "reason": "<p>A step of two from the odd base visits exactly the positive odd indices.</p>"
      },
      "contentSha256": "a7c35751dc15669c76d30149d5aeb617f0e1b7abb474f680fb87a6d0e4e0e1fd"
    }
